id: monica-api-source-freshness
title: Verify bundled Monica API source freshness
description: Add a machine-readable read-only command that verifies the checked-in Monica stable 4.x API snapshot against the current authoritative upstream branch so humans and agents can distinguish proven-current coverage from stale bundled evidence.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[8]: agent-ux,api-contracts,api-research,documentation,provenance,read-only,schema,upstream-verification
created_at: "2026-07-25T00:14:08.722Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T00:56:02.313Z"
deadline: "2026-07-27T00:14:08.722Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-25T00:56:01.296Z"
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: "The CLI exposes documented api-research source-status help and machine output in every supported format; The command verifies the current monicahq/monica 4.x head against checked-in provenance and classifies current, stale, and unavailable states separately; --fail-on-stale exits 2 only for proven drift and preserves a structured payload; A registered output schema validates all source-status states and real CLI output; Agent catalogs and read-only E2E include the new command without enabling any mutation; Latest compatible pm-changelog is installed and latest global pm-cli use is documented without weakening npm peer resolution; Exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, 100 percent docstrings, all help leaves, package smoke, security, privacy, duplication, PM, and changelog gates pass; No private Monica data or credentials enter Git, PM history, logs, commits, or PR text"
definition_of_ready: Authoritative upstream branch and snapshot provenance are identifiable; existing all-status PM lineage has been searched; local settings are read-only and private.
goal: Continuously verifiable stable Monica API compatibility
objective: Make API coverage freshness independently provable by the CLI
value: Prevents agents from treating a complete but stale API snapshot as current
impact: Raises confidence in automation and future API parity work without touching CRM data
outcome: A schema-backed freshness verdict suitable for local use and CI
why_now: "The latest research revalidated the snapshot manually, revealing that the proof is not yet executable by CLI consumers"
parent: monica-platform
reviewer: unbraind
risk: high
confidence: 95
sprint: 2026-07-api-provenance
release: next
reporter: codex-root
severity: high
environment: Monica stable 4.x public GitHub repository; monica-cli 2026.7.24-2; Bun 1.3.11; Node 22+
repro_steps: Run monica api-research summary and inspect source metadata; there is no command that verifies the bundled commit against the current upstream 4.x head or fails CI when it drifts.
resolution: "Added a public upstream source-status command with current, stale, and unavailable classification; published its schema and agent/read-only contracts; upgraded pm-changelog; corrected API research documentation; remediated the newly disclosed brace-expansion advisory; and recorded first-party PM extension warnings upstream."
expected_result: "Agents can independently verify that the bundled API reference is current, stale, or temporarily unverifiable using a safe structured CLI command."
actual_result: "The actual monica CLI verifies the bundled Monica 4.x commit against the public authoritative branch, honors the inherited request timeout, reports current today, emits validated TOON/JSON/YAML/table/Markdown, exposes a structured CI gate, and remains mutation-safe. Coverage passes with 854 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 and 587/587 documented exports. Live read-only acceptance passes 44 commands, classifies 53 systemic host failures as expected, blocks five writes before network access, and has zero unexpected failures."
affected_version: 2026.7.24-2
fixed_version: 2026.7.25
component: api-research
regression: false
customer_impact: A future upstream route change could leave automation confidently using outdated coverage until a manual audit notices.
